From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:59:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] kk: MESA_KK_DEBUG=fault names where a failed command buffer
 stopped and what each encoder did

The first failure 0154 logged on the phone (The Witcher 3 1.32, PLA-880)
was "Caused GPU Hang Error (kIOGPUCommandBufferCallbackErrorHang)" 28 ms
into a command buffer of 15 encoders: three render passes of the game,
eleven passes of one draw (a mip chain, DXVK's GenerateMips by blits)
and a copy. Neither Metal nor the trail said which encoder the GPU stopped
in, or what any of them rendered to and read.

With MESA_KK_DEBUG=fault each trail entry now also holds:
- two GPU timestamps, written when the encoder starts and when it ends,
  into a ring of 8192 in a counter heap (none while a GPU capture is
  armed: 0044). A failed commit reads them on the CPU and prints each
  encoder's gpu=+start..+end ms after the commit, "-" for none written
  since, and UNFINISHED for one that started and did not end: where the
  GPU stopped;
- the attachments of a render encoder: image, VkFormat, level, layers,
  extent, samples, load and store op and the store action Metal got, and
  whether the encoder continues a render pass begun in an earlier one;
- the pipelines it drew or dispatched with and how often, by the first 16
  hex digits of their MSL hash ([kk-compile] msl=), "driver-internal" for
  libkk's; the largest direct draw;
- the vk_meta operation that made it (meta:vkCmdBlitImage2, ...);
- the timestamp fence it waited for, the resolves encoded after it, a
  queue barrier before its vertex stage and its end barrier;
- a sampled, storage or input attachment descriptor of its draws that
  names one of its own attachments at overlapping levels and layers
  (FEEDBACK), found by looking up each descriptor's texture in a map of
  image views by GPU resource ID once after each change of the graphics
  descriptors or the encoder.

Each submit's semaphore waits, command buffers and signals are kept too
(16 submits), and a failure prints the failed command buffer's submit
and the two before it with each event's signaled value now.

The trail moves into the commit instead of being copied.

Linear: PLA-880
Class: diagnostics
Evidence: build/mesa-host-test/kk-fault-test.c (mock Metal: a failed command buffer of blits); PLA-880 (the phone's first [kk-fault] lines)
Offered-upstream: no
